": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The payments incident is mitigated, but I stopped short of one step.\n\n**What I did**\n- **Rolled back `payments-worker` from v3.4.0 to v3.3.0** in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). This is the last release that was healthy in production. It now reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate, down from 18%.\n- **Opened incident INC-0002 (SEV2)** against `payments-worker`. It paged on-call. The summary covers the v3.4.0 regression, the rollback, and the payments-api observation.\n\n**What didn't go as planned**\n- My first attempt was against `payments-api` (v5.1.0 \u2192 v5.0.0). A human reviewer denied it, saying the problem was in `payments-worker`, so I didn't retry it. The change was not applied.\n- The first incident request timed out, and the incident list showed no incident created. I opened the replacement incident against `payments-worker` instead.\n\n**Still open**\n- `payments-api` is still on v5.1.0, reporting unhealthy with an 18% error rate. Its error rate matches `payments-worker`'s pre-rollback rate, so it may be a downstream symptom, but I haven't confirmed that. I didn't roll it back because the reviewer rejected that. Someone should confirm whether it needs its own action.", "type": "text"}]}]}